<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A two-state button that stays pressed - bold on, bold off.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/toggle)

<%= embed UI::TogglePreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Toggle(pressed: true, aria_label: "Bold") { |toggle| Button(**toggle, variant: :outline, icon: true) { Icon(:bold) } }
```

`Toggle` is behavior only - a `<button aria-pressed>` with no styling. A block that takes an argument receives its
attributes (Appica's `render` prop), so it becomes any [Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>), which already paints the
pressed state through `data-pressed`. A block without an argument renders a plain `<button>` you style yourself.
To group toggles, see [Toggle Group](<%= page_path(:toggle_group) %>).

